l","hostId":"muse-1","side":"front","start":0.05,"end":0.52,"elevation":0.5,"height":2.3,"color":"#F5F0E8","graphic":"frame","graphicColor":"#111111","text":"SEE WHAT YOU SEE"},{"id":"ws-north-hey","hostType":"wall","hostId":"muse-1","side":"front","start":0.53,"end":0.95,"elevation":0.5,"height":2.3,"color":"#111111","graphic":"stripe","graphicColor":"#8A5A3B","text":"Hey Meta, take a photo"},{"id":"ws-south-wood","hostType":"wall","hostId":"muse-8","side":"back","start":0.05,"end":0.95,"elevation":0.3,"height":2,"color":"#8A5A3B","graphic":"frame","graphicColor":"#111111","text":"SEONGSU ALLEY"},{"id":"ws-video-live","hostType":"wall","hostId":"muse-10","side":"back","start":0.1,"end":0.9,"elevation":0.4,"height":2.2,"color":"#0E0E14","graphic":"stripe","graphicColor":"#F5F0E8","text":"LIVE FROM YOUR EYES"},{"id":"ws-west-frame","hostType":"wall","hostId":"muse-6","side":"back","start":0.15,"end":0.85,"elevation":0.4,"height":2.4,"color":"#111111","graphic":"frame","graphicColor":"#F5F0E8","text":"AI GLASSES STUDIO"},{"id":"ws-east-plaster","hostType":"wall","hostId":"muse-4","side":"front","start":0.1,"end":0.9,"elevation":0.4,"height":2.2,"color":"#E8DCC8","graphic":"frame","graphicColor":"#8A5A3B","text":"OPEN EAR LISTENING"}],"sources":[{"kind":"brief","name":"Try. Capture. Share. · Pop-up brief","text":"An independently authored fictional demo, not an official Meta event, commission or partnership. Dimensions and quantities are design assumptions, not measured capacity or safety validation.\n\nObjective: Give first-time visitors in their twenties and thirties a 20-minute journey through trying on glasses, hands-free photography, open-ear listening and sharing with friends. Use the entire approximately 590 m² ground floor in Seongsu.\n\nProgram: One check-in counter; two four-seat fitting bars with mirrors; a photo walk with three photo spots; an eight-seat listening lounge; two semi-enclosed Messenger demo booths; one shared photo wall; one consultation and pickup counter.\n\nJourney: Angled entrance → check-in → fitting bars → photo walk between columns → listening lounge → Messenger booths and photo wall in the annex → consultation and pickup. Keep the main route at least 1.5m clear. Use the south service door and storage for staff and stock.\n\nDrawing: The north main hall is approximately 32 × 15m with a 4.2m assumed ceiling; the southeast annex is approximately 18 × 7m with a 3.6m assumed ceiling. Preserve the three 0.6m square columns. Keep the north shopfront and east windows visible. Ceiling heights are drawing assumptions; suspended loads are unreviewed. Do not furnish the toilets or storage.\n\nDirection: Warm off-white surfaces, black lines inspired by acetate frames, and bright street-like lighting. Low walls, plants and signs create small Seongsu-inspired photo scenes.\n\nRequest: Design the entire floor with actual furniture and partitions, connecting the experiences with a one-way visitor journey."},{"kind":"brand","name":"Ray-Ban Meta · Brand reference","text":"AI glasses with a camera, open-ear speakers and microphones. The demo interprets hands-free capture, listening and communication as fitting bars, a photo walk and a listening lounge."},{"kind":"brand","name":"Messenger · Brand reference","text":"Messaging and voice/video conversations with friends and groups. The demo interprets these as hands-free message and call booths, followed by a shared visitor photo wall."},{"kind":"concept","name":"AI glasses fitting bar · Authored concept","text":"A long off-white fitting counter with a black worktop and base, approximately 4m × 1.2m and 1.05m high. A walnut-toned tray holds demonstration glasses; three black-framed mirror panels stand behind it. Three black stools with brown cushions and a brass foot rail illustrate fitting, mirror checks and staff guidance in one furniture unit. This does not reproduce the product design."},{"kind":"brand","name":"Ray-Ban Meta Korea launch · News reference","text":"Bookmarked Meta news about the May 2026 Korean launch of Ray-Ban Meta and Oakley Meta. Used only as context for a first-time visitor experience in Korea."}]}